   "subject": "Re:",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>Further to Tom&#39;s answer you can also do it with geom_polygon and coord_polar:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reshape2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>pd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iris</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">51</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">101</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># express the values as a fraction of max value</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>pd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>pd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">melt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> melt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># duplicate the last entry to get the polygon to &quot;join up&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>pd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">melt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rbind</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">melt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> pd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">melt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">melt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> variable</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> value</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> colour </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Species</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Species</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  coord_polar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  geom_polygon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fill </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  ylim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br>g</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>I see the point about these plots being misleading depending on the order of the `variable` factor. For better or worse I&#39;ve also seen them &#39;sports analytics&#39;. </div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div><br></div><div>(another) Tom</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
